[{"id":"MaU_8","ref":"8","section":"Oṃ and its sound elements","sa":["सोऽयमात्माध्यक्षरमोङ्कारोऽधिमात्रं पादा मात्रा मात्राश्च पादा","अकार उकारो मकार इति ॥ ८॥"],"iast":["so’yamātmādhyakṣaramoṅkāro’dhimātraṃ pādā mātrā mātrāśca pādā","akāra ukāro makāra iti ॥ 8॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Now this the Self, as to the imperishable Word, is OM; and as to the letters, His parts are the letters and the letters are His parts, namely, A U M.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 195","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["सः","saḥ","he","saḥ"],["अयम्","ayam","this","ayam"],["आत्मा","ātmā","Self","ātmā"],["अध्यक्षरम्","adhyakṣaram","with reference to the syllable","adhyakṣaram"],["ओङ्कारः","oṅkāraḥ","the utterance Oṃ","oṅkāraḥ"],["अधिमात्रम्","adhimātram","with reference to the sound elements","adhimātram"],["पादाः","pādāḥ","quarters","pādāḥ"],["मात्राः","mātrāḥ","sound elements","mātrāḥ"],["मात्राः","mātrāḥ","sound elements","mātrāḥ"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["पादाः","pādāḥ","quarters","pādāḥ"],["अकारः","akāraḥ","the sound A","akāraḥ"],["उकारः","ukāraḥ","the sound U","ukāraḥ"],["मकारः","makāraḥ","the sound M","makāraḥ"],["इति","iti","thus","iti"]],"tr":{"text":"That same Self, from the point of view of the syllable, is Om, and viewed from the stand point of the letters, the quarters are the letters, and the letters are the quarters. The letters are a, u and m.","by":"Vidyavachaspati V. Panoli","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mandukyopanisad/5.8.mp3","whole":[166.58,186.22]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":9,"up":"mandukya"}]